class Solution {
public:
    int maximumUnits(vector<vector<int>>& boxTypes, int truckSize) {
        sort(boxTypes.begin(), boxTypes.end(),
             [](vector<int>& a, vector<int>& b) {
                 return a[1] > b[1];
             });

        int units = 0;

        for (auto& box : boxTypes) {
            int boxes = min(truckSize, box[0]);
            units += boxes * box[1];
            truckSize -= boxes;

            if (truckSize == 0)
                break;
        }

        return units;
    }
};

**Intuition:**  
Prioritize boxes having more units per box.  
This maximizes the total units within the limited truck capacity.

**Algorithm:**  
Sort box types in decreasing order of units per box.  
Take as many boxes as possible from each type until the truck is full.

**Complexity:**  
Time: **O(n log n)**  
Space: **O(1)** auxiliary space
